# Cursor Editor — Data Privacy & Local vs Cloud Decisions

## Overview

Understanding Cursor's data flow is critical for developers and organizations handling sensitive code. Cursor operates across multiple environments: your local machine, Cursor's cloud infrastructure, and third-party model providers (Anthropic, OpenAI, etc.). This document explains where data flows, what is retained, and how to control privacy settings.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph local [Local Environment]
        A[Cursor IDE] --> B[Local Agent Runtime]
        B --> C[Your Machine]
    end
    
    subgraph cloud [Cursor Cloud]
        D[cursor.com] --> E[Cloud VM Runtime]
        E --> F[Cloud Agent Runs]
    end
    
    subgraph provider [Model Providers]
        G[Anthropic API] --> H[Claude Models]
        I[OpenAI API] --> J[GPT Models]
        K[Custom Endpoint] --> L[Local/Own Models]
    end
    
    A -->|"API calls with code"| G
    A -->|"API calls with code"| I
    A -->|"API calls with code"| K
    
    B -->|"Local code stays local"| C
    E -->|"Code in VM"| F
    F -->|"API calls with code"| G
    F -->|"API calls with code"| I
    
    A -->|"Telemetry"| D
    A -->|"Session transcripts"| D
    D -->|"Analytics"| M[Cursor Analytics]
```

