## Local Processing

### When Code Stays on Your Machine

The agent processes code locally in these scenarios:

| Scenario | Processing Location | Data Leaves Machine? |
|----------|-------------------|---------------------|
| **Tab Completions (local model)** | Your machine | No (if using local model) |
| **Ask Mode (read-only)** | Your machine (for file reads) | No (files are sent to provider for generation) |
| **Custom/local model endpoints** | Your configured endpoint | Depends on endpoint |
| **Ollama/vLLM local inference** | Your machine | No |
| **File operations (Read, Write, Shell)** | Your machine | No (except for API calls to model providers) |

### Local-Only Configurations

To ensure code stays on your machine, use local or self-hosted models:

```json
{
  // Local model for Tab completions (zero data egress)
  "cursor.agent.tabProvider": "custom",
  "cursor.agent.tabModel": "codegemma:7b",
  "cursor.agent.tabBaseUrl": "http://localhost:11434/v1",
  
  // Self-hosted inference server
  "cursor.agent.agentProvider": "custom",
  "cursor.agent.agentModel": "your-local-model",
  "cursor.agent.agentBaseUrl": "http://inference-server.internal/v1",
  
  // Disable telemetry
  "telemetry.telemetryLevel": "off",
  "cursor.telemetry.enabled": false
}
```

### Supported Local Processing Providers

| Provider | Type | Data Leaves Machine? |
|----------|------|---------------------|
| **Ollama** | Local GPU inference | No |
| **vLLM** | Local/self-hosted serving | No (if self-hosted) |
| **LM Studio** | Local inference | No |
| **LocalAI** | Self-hosted OpenAI-compatible | No (if self-hosted) |
| **Together AI** | Cloud-hosted | Yes (to Together) |
| **Anthropic** | Cloud-hosted | Yes (to Anthropic) |
| **OpenAI** | Cloud-hosted | Yes (to OpenAI) |

