## Telemetry

### What Cursor Collects

| Category | Data Points | PII? | Anonymized? |
|----------|------------|------|-------------|
| **Usage metrics** | Feature usage, session counts | No | Yes |
| **Performance data** | Response times, error rates | No | Yes |
| **Agent behavior** | Tool selection frequency, decision patterns | No | Yes |
| **Crash reports** | Stack traces, error messages | No (code snippets may appear) | Partially |
| **System info** | OS, Cursor version, architecture | No | Yes |

### Crash Report Examples

```json
// Anonymized crash report
{
  "timestamp": "2026-06-11T10:00:00Z",
  "cursorVersion": "1.0.0",
  "os": "windows",
  "agentId": "bc_abc123",
  "errorType": "APIError",
  "errorMessage": "Rate limit exceeded",
  "toolCall": "Shell",
  "stackTrace": "Error: Rate limit exceeded... (truncated)"
}

// Note: Code content in error messages may be included
// but is stripped of identifying information when possible
```

### Disabling Telemetry

```json
{
  // Disable all telemetry
  "telemetry.telemetryLevel": "off",
  
  // Disable crash reporting
  "telemetry.crashReporting.enabled": false,
  
  // Disable usage analytics
  "telemetry.analytics.enabled": false,
  
  // Disable session recording
  "telemetry.sessionRecording.enabled": false
}
```

```bash
# CLI alternative
claude --disable-telemetry "Your prompt"
```

