## Compliance Considerations

### SOC 2

Cursor's cloud infrastructure follows SOC 2 Type II practices:

| Control | Implementation |
|---------|---------------|
| **Encryption at rest** | AES-256 for stored data |
| **Encryption in transit** | TLS 1.3 for all API calls |
| **Access controls** | Role-based access for Cursor employees |
| **Audit logging** | All infrastructure changes logged |
| **Data segregation** | Team data isolated by workspace |

### GDPR

For EU-based users and data:

| Requirement | Cursor Implementation |
|-------------|---------------------|
| **Right to access** | Export your data via cursor.com dashboard |
| **Right to erasure** | Request deletion of all data via settings or support |
| **Data minimization** | Only essential telemetry collected |
| **Data localization** | Available via Enterprise tier (EU regions) |
| **Processing records** | Available via DPA (Data Processing Agreement) |

### HIPAA

**Cursor is not HIPAA-compliant out of the box.** For healthcare organizations:

1. Contact Cursor sales for HIPAA-capable Enterprise deployment
2. Use self-hosted model endpoints (Ollama, vLLM) for PHI data
3. Disable cloud agent processing entirely
4. Implement local-only processing for all AI operations
5. Sign BAA (Business Associate Agreement) with Cursor

