## Enterprise Settings

### MDM Policies (macOS/Windows)

Cursor supports MDM policy enforcement for enterprise deployments:

```json
// MDM policy override file (managed by IT)
{
  "enterprise": {
    "managedSettings": {
      "cursor.agent.mode": "agent",
      "cursor.agent.chatModel": "claude-sonnet-4-20250514",
      "cursor.agent.contextWindow": 128000,
      "telemetry.telemetryLevel": "minimal",
      "cursor.cloud.enabled": true,
      "cursor.agent.attribution.enabled": true
    },
    "unmodifiableSettings": [
      "telemetry.telemetryLevel",
      "cursor.cloud.enabled",
      "cursor.agent.chatModel"
    ]
  }
}
```

### Admin Controls

| Control | Admin Action | User Impact |
|---------|-------------|-------------|
| **Model restrictions** | Set allowed models list | Users cannot select other models |
| **Telemetry enforcement** | Set telemetry level | Users cannot disable |
| **Cloud agent policy** | Enable/disable cloud agent | All users affected |
| **Data retention** | Set retention period | All sessions deleted after period |
| **API key management** | Distribute team keys | No personal key needed |

### Enterprise Deployment Checklist

- [ ] MDM policies configured
- [ ] Team workspace created on cursor.com
- [ ] Team API keys generated and distributed
- [ ] Data retention policy documented
- [ ] Local-only mode available for sensitive teams
- [ ] HIPAA BAA signed (if applicable)
- [ ] SOC 2 report obtained
- [ ] GDPR compliance verified
- [ ] Admin training completed
- [ ] User training completed

